  "fps": {
    "target": 30.0,
    "method": "fps_sustained: the output PTS sequence at the v4l2sink sink pad is exact over the window (every tick index once, in order), the frame count is within max(0.1 %, 1 frame) of the contract rate times the window, and the deviation of each frame's sink-pad arrival from its PTS grid instant (clock start + PTS) spans at most one output period plus a jitter allowance (deviation.limit_ms). A deviation span of at most one period bounds every wall-clock 1 s window to the contract rate +-1 frame; sliding_1s reports the fewest and most frames actually seen in any 1 s window. With --consumer in measured runs the same is required of the consumer, by the output PTS stamped into each frame. The phase-locked clock emits each tick within one period before its timestamp, following the camera, so the grid-window figure (output_grid: windows on one mean arrival phase) is kept for comparison only.",
